  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strong tripartite constituents (Workers), and influential, inclusive social dialogue</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Viet Nam, industrial relations, collective bargaining and wider social dialogue have been evolving in recent years, especially in light of the revised labour code in 2019. 

The ILO supports the strengthening of workers&#x2019; representation in Viet Nam, aligned with national labour law reforms and application of the international labour standards. It focuses on building the capacity of the Trade Union to better represent workers&#x2019; rights, especially in the context of the 2019 Labour Code and revised Trade Union Law. Key goals include improving collective bargaining, wage negotiation, and social dialogue at all levels.  In partnership with the Viet Nam Conferderation of Labour (VGCL), the ILO promotes alignment with national and global labour standards and addresses emerging issues like climate change, just transition, jobs and social protection, and human rights&#x2014;placing workers at the centre of a sustainable development agenda. The key benefiaries are vulnerable and informal workers, as well as trade union representatives, to ensure wider access to protection and participation in industrial relations.</narrative>
  </description>
